    <li><a name="n4" id="n4"></a>According to the 2015 Program for International Student Assessment (PISA) by  the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development (OECD), the U.S.  ranks 19th in science, 20th in reading and 31st in mathematics out of 35 OECD  countries. An average of the scores across the three categories places the U.S.  in 24th.</li>
    <li><a name="n5" id="n5"></a>According to the Survey of Adult Skills (Program for International Assessment  of Adult Competencies) (2012, 2015) by the OECD, the U.S. ranks 17th in  literacy and 23rd in math out of 29 countries and 15th in problem solving in  technology-rich environments out of 26 countries. An average of scores across  the literacy and math categories places the U.S. 20th.</li>
